## CORE RULES

**NO MOCKS, NO SHORTCUTS, NO HACKS**
- All implementations must be production-ready
- Complete features fully or not at all
- No temporary solutions, workarounds, or "quick fixes"
- No simplified versions, hardcoded values, or debug-only code
- No TODO placeholders that become permanent

**DEPENDENCY MANAGEMENT**
- If Feature A needs Feature B, stop A and complete B first
- All dependencies must be fully implemented before proceeding
- No partial implementations allowed
- Maintain clean dependency hierarchy

**ERROR HANDLING**
- All error conditions must return proper errors
- Code must be deterministic and predictable
- No silent failures or undefined behavior
- Fallbacks require explicit approval and must have a real reason to exist
- Return errors when conditions are not satisfied

**TESTING**
- All tests must use real implementations (no mocks)
- Complete coverage including edge cases
- Integration tests required
- No test-only code in production builds

## PROHIBITED

❌ Mock implementations
❌ Placeholder functions
❌ Hardcoded test values
❌ "We'll fix it later" approach
❌ Skipping proper error handling
❌ Implementing features in isolation
❌ Simplified implementations
❌ fallbacks without explicit aproval an solid justification


## REQUIRED

1. **Complete Prerequisites First**
   - Identify all dependencies
   - Implement dependencies completely
   - No circular dependencies

2. **Full Implementation Only**
   - Implement complete features
   - No shortcuts or simplifications
   - Include proper error handling
   - Add comprehensive real tests

3. **Real Integration**
   - Integrate with actual implementations
   - Test all scenarios with real code
   - Verify end-to-end functionality

4. **Production Ready**
   - Follow Apple platform best practices
   - Implement security best practices
   - Optimize for real-world performance
   - Well-documented code

## WORKFLOW

1. Analyze full requirements
2. Complete all dependencies first
3. Implement complete feature
4. Test with real implementations
5. Code review for compliance

## AGENT INSTRUCTIONS

- Stop and implement dependencies when needed
- Never use mocks or placeholders
- Handle all error conditions properly
- Write real tests with real implementations
- Ask for clarification and never make assumptions
- Ensure production readiness at all times

## CODE QUALITY TOOLS
```bash
swiftlint --strict --config .swiftlint.yml
```
- Treats warnings as errors
- Enforces coding standards
- Must pass before any PR/commit

```bash
swiftformat .
```
- Automatically formats Swift code
- Consistent code style
- Must be run before any PR/commit

**Usage:**
- Run both tools at the end of every task
- Fix all issues before proceeding
- Ensure code is properly formatted and linted
- No exceptions - these are mandatory
